ta traveling  between customers devices and our data  centers is encrypted using HTTPS TLS so  transport layer security and in fact  Google was the first major cloud  provider to enable TLS encryption and  this homogeneous environment is  maintained by proprietary software that  continually monitors the system's  binaries for any binary modification for  our teams to be successful they must  have advanced real-time visibility into  the status and functionality of our  infrastructure as you know to say that  Google is obsessed with data might be a  little bit of an understatement so our  teams build systems that allow us to  monitor everything we've built  world-class monitoring and control  systems for all functional areas from  the servers and storage and network to  the electrical distribution the  mechanical cooling systems and the  security systems we're monitoring all  aspects of performance and operations  from chip to chiller and I said mint  and energy efficiency is at the heart of  our sustainability program you know we  believe that the best energy saved is  the energy not consumed in the first  place that's why we pioneered hyper  efficient computing systems and data  centers and that's why our data centers  consume on average only half of the  energy of a typical enterprise data  center what makes us really stand out in  this regard is how we've applied machine  learning to drive energy efficiency even  further if you've been in the keynote  speeches over the last couple of days  you've heard how much emphasis Google  has been placing on our machine learning  programs well you can imagine our data  centers are very large and complex where  the electrical and mechanical control  systems are all working together to  deliver optimal performance but because  of the sheer number of interactions and  possible settings for all of these  systems it's impossible for you know us  mere mortals to visualize what the best  way to set up the data center controls  are for those specific operating  conditions and to do it in real time  however really it's fairly trivial for  the computers to crunch through all  these possible scenarios and find the  optimal settings so over the past couple  of years we've developed an algorithm  and we've trained it with billions of  data points from all of our data centers  all over the world we now use machine  learning models to help visualize this  data so the operations teams can set up  the data center electrical and cooling  plants for the most optimal efficient  performance on any given day it's also  used considering up to 19 independent  variables like the weather outside the  temperature the humidity the wind  direction the wind speed all of these  things go into how efficient a data  center runs but without a machine  learning model it's almost impossible  for the operations teams to to try and  adjust that real-time so in partnership  with our colleagues at deep mind our  data center team built models to  recognize and learn  from these patterns in the large amounts  of operational data that we collect  every day anyhow we just restoring it  and not really using it that well so now  this is you know over some trial and  error and perfecting the model the model  is now over ninety nine point six  percent accurate and predicting our PE  and PE is power usage effectiveness it's  a measure of data center efficiency and  it has helped us to identify up to forty  percent savings in the data center  cooling overhead this equates to an  overall fifteen fifteen percent  reduction in our PE which you know may  not seem like a lot but if you think  about the hundreds of megawatts of data  center capacity that we have online  every year that is equated to several  tens of millions of dollars in energy  savings per year but you might wonder  why why do I care why do I care if your  data centers are efficient well one of  the reasons why you care is because our  operating costs are directly related to  the efficiency of our data centers our  pricing on Google cloud is directly  related to our operating costs so the  more efficient we are internally the  more of that savings we can pass through  to you we can offer the most high  performance lowest cost public cloud  available and leverage  strengthen this machine-learning we've  succeeded in increasing the overall  efficiency of our data center fleet this  makes Google the data center you need  the one that you really can't afford to  be without high performance computing  available around the world secure  reliable where you need it when you need  it and how you need it  you
 

